/*!
    \page whatsnew612.html
    \title What's New in Qt 6.12
    \ingroup whatsnewqt6
    \brief Lists the new features in Qt 6.12.
    \meta sortkey 612

    \section1 New and Restored Modules in Qt 6.12

    Qt 6.12 adds the following modules and tools:

    \list
    \endlist

    \section1 New Features in Qt 6.12

    \section2 Qt Bluetooth Module
    \list
      \li The Android backend now respects the advertising minimum and
          maximum interval parameters provided via \l QLowEnergyAdvertisingParameters
          when starting the BTLE advertising.
    \endlist

    \section2 Qt Canvas Painter Module
    \list
      \li The \l{Qt Canvas Painter} module is moving out of Technology Preview
          state, and is now fully maintained (supported).
      \li The module gained \l{QtCanvas2D}, a new QML API backed by Qt Canvas
          Painter. This API remains in technology preview.
      \li \l{QCanvasPath} gained an
          \l{QCanvasPath::addPath(QStringView, const QTransform &)}{addPath()}
          overload for parsing SVG path strings directly.
      \li \l{QCanvasPainter} gained \l{QCanvasPainter::FillRule} and
          \l{QCanvasPainter::setFillRule()} to support the EvenOdd fill
          rule for path fills.
      \li \l{QCanvasGradient} gained
          \l{QCanvasGradient::setImage()}{setImage()} to create gradients
          directly from an image.
      \li \l{QCanvasRadialGradient} gained constructors and
          \l{QCanvasRadialGradient::setInnerCenterPosition()}{setInnerCenterPosition()}
          /
          \l{QCanvasRadialGradient::setOuterCenterPosition()}{setOuterCenterPosition()}
          to support non-symmetric (two-center) radial gradients.
    \endlist

    \section2 Qt Core Module
    \list
      \li \l{QRangeModel}'s \l{QRangeModel::}{RowOptions} and
          \l{QRangeModel::}{ItemAccess} customization points were extended to
          support \c headerData(), and per-row and per-item \c flags().
          \l{QRangeModel} gained \l{QRangeModel#Drag'n'drop handling}
          {drag'n'drop handling} support with custom and type-safe mime type
          handling in both customization points, and with
          \l{QRangeModel::}{supportedDragActions} and
          \l{QRangeModel::}{supportedDropActions} properties.
          \l{QRangeModel} now also implements \l{QRangeModel::}{sort()} with
          support of a \l{QRangeModel::}{sortCollator} for locale-aware sorting,
          and \l{QRangeModel::}{match()} for fast content matching.
      \li Added \l{qSharedPointerStaticCast} as a new free function for
          static casts of \l{QSharedPointer}.
      \li \l{QSortFilterProxyModel} gained the
          \l{QSortFilterProxyModel::DataChangeRelevance}{DataChangeRelevance}
          enum and the virtual
          \l{QSortFilterProxyModel::dataChangeRelevances()}{dataChangeRelevances()}
          method, allowing subclasses to control whether a source
          \c dataChanged signal triggers re-filtering or re-sorting.
      \li The new \l{QAbstractItemModel::compareData()} is a new protected API for
          comparing two QVariants in a way that is specifically designed for item
          view use cases.
      \li \l{qfloat16} gained increment and decrement operators and a
          unary \l{qfloat16::operator+()}{operator+}.
      \li \l{QVariant} gained constructors from rvalue references.
      \li \l{QMap} and \l{QMultiMap} now implement all six relational
          operators.
      \li \l{QVarLengthArray} gained
          \l{QVarLengthArray::removeAt()}{removeAt()}, matching the
          \l{QList} API.
      \li \l{QTimeZone} now accepts CLDR-canonical IANA alias IDs in its
          constructor and in
          \l{QTimeZone::isTimeZoneIdAvailable()}{isTimeZoneIdAvailable()}.
          \l{QTimeZone::availableTimeZoneIds()} now includes those aliases.
      \li \l{QFile::copy()} now accepts an optional
          \l{QFileDevice::Permissions} argument.
          \l{QSaveFile} now defers applying the requested permissions until
          \l{QSaveFile::commit()}{commit()}.
      \li \l{Qt::compareThreeWay()} gained an overload for
          \c{std::pair}.
      \li \l{QCalendarPermission} gained a
          \l{QCalendarPermission::AccessMode}{WriteOnly} access mode.
      \li \l{QFileSystemWatcher} can now use \c inotify on FreeBSD 15 and
          later.
      \li \l{QStandardPaths} on macOS now includes the system-wide
          \c{/Library/Preferences} directory in
          \l{QStandardPaths::standardLocations()}{standardLocations()}.
          On iOS, \l{QStandardPaths::}{PublicShareLocation} returns the correct path and
          \l{QStandardPaths::}{TemplatesLocation} is properly reported as unsupported.
      \li \l{QEasingCurve} gained
          \l{QEasingCurve::cubicBezier()}{cubicBezier()}, a convenience
          helper for creating cubic Bezier easing curves.
      \li \l{QJsonObject} gained \l{QJsonObject::cbegin()}{cbegin()} and
          \l{QJsonObject::cend()}{cend()} STL-style const iterators.
          \l{QJsonDocument} gained rvalue constructors from
          \l{QJsonArray} and \l{QJsonObject}.
    \endlist

